## §2 Method

**Unit of analysis.** One sealed goal = the **complete post-seal artifact set** PAEOS actually
holds for it — not the single review file. Probing only `reviews/tasks/B0.x_review.md` would
have produced a falsely pessimistic verdict, because that file is a 10-point PASS/FAIL
checklist and is the *thinnest* artifact of the four. The artifact set probed per goal:

| Artifact | Role | §6.1b source? |
|---|---|---|
| `spec/PAEOS-8-runtime-implementation-playbook.md` §10 row | task definition: objective, deps, acceptance criteria, verification method, actor | not listed |
| `docs/B0.x-constitutional-review.md` | CER-4 / FP-3 close-out: evidence table, design, six questions, adversary pass, founder verdict | **the de-facto L15 artifact** |
| `reviews/tasks/B0.x_review.md` | 10-point constitutional checklist | not listed |
| `ledger/debt/DEBT-000x.md` | compromise, reason, ideal solution, repayment, impact, founder ratification | not listed |

**Node types probed.** The seven SAEOS-1 §6.1b emission types (`Decision`, `TradeOff`,
`Option`, `Constraint`, `Component`, `Scar`, `EvidenceRef`) plus `Outcome`. `Outcome` is
formally S3 (§6.1b rule 3, L17/L19) but is scored here because Ω2 depends on it and because
the corpus turned out to carry it — see §4.

**Slots.** Each node type contributes the §4.2 universal envelope (16 slots) plus its §4.3
type-specific content. `confidence` is excluded from the denominator: §4.2 declares it
**DERIVED, never authored**, so it is not an extraction target and cannot fail.

| Type | Type-specific slots |
|---|---|
| Decision | `choice`, `context`, `alternatives`, `rationale`, `constitutional_basis` (5) |
| Option | `candidate`, `disposition`, `why` (3) |
| Constraint | `limit`, `kind` (2) |
| TradeOff | `axis`, `party_a`, `party_b`, `resolution` (4) |
| Component | `name`, `kind` (2) |
| Scar | `root_cause`, `detection_signature`, `guard_action` (3) |
| EvidenceRef | `hash`, `uri`, `kind`, `reverification` (4) |
| Outcome | `disposition`, `observation_window`, `measurement` (3) |

**16 envelope + 26 type-specific = 42 slots per goal · 3 goals = 126 slots.**

**Scoring.** **E** = extractable (recoverable mechanically, no invention). **P** = partial
(recoverable for *some* instances, or some sub-fields, or requires generative compression
rather than transcription). **A** = absent (no amount of parsing recovers it; supplying it
would be fabrication).

A field scores **E only if it is recoverable for every node instance the goal should
produce** — not merely for the best instance. This is the correct standard for a *lossless
round-trip* criterion and it is deliberately harsh.

**Formula.**

```
loss_ratio = (A + 0.5·P) / (E + P + A)
```

**Universal envelope — all three goals.**

