## §7 Assumptions surfaced (PAEOS-6 register method)

Assumptions this probe **makes**, in the `Ω-NN` form of `reviews/6-hidden-assumptions.md` §B.
Each is load-bearing on the verdict and each is stated so it can be attacked.

**Ω-P1 — B0.0–B0.2 are pre-lifecycle bootstrap tasks, not L15-sealed goals. [most severe]**
They come from PAEOS-8 §10's Phase-0 table and predate `operations/ENGINEERING_LIFECYCLE.md`'s
L01–L19 stages. They therefore never ran L04 (candidate set), L06 (trade-off matrix), L08
(architecture set) or L11 (implementation contract) — the four artifacts §6.1b names as
`Option`, `TradeOff`, `Component` and `Constraint` sources. **This probe measures the
substitute artifacts, not the specified ones.** Direction of bias is genuinely unknown: a real
L15 goal should score *better* on `Option`/`TradeOff`/`Constraint` (those stages emit them by
construction), which would make 0.25 pessimistic — but that is an argument from specification,
and this probe exists precisely because arguments from specification are what A8 distrusts.
**This is the probe's largest threat to validity.** *Repayment:* re-run this method against the
first true L15-sealed goal before S1 is declared passed. If F1's TradeOff loss does not fall
below 0.30 there, **P2 escalates from precondition to NO-GO**.

